  "goodToKnow": "Rechtsextrem means far-right or right-wing extremist: rechtsextreme Gewalt, eine rechtsextreme Szene. In German politics there's an official distinction: rechtsextrem means hostile to the constitutional order, while rechtspopulistisch and rechtsradikal are used more loosely. The Verfassungsschutz (domestic intelligence) monitors groups it classifies as gesichert rechtsextrem (confirmed far-right extremist). The opposite is linksextrem. Note: rechts here means right, not Recht (law)."
